{"module":"lawmaking","voice":"male","duration":179.6,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"How a bill becomes law, and how this one could","start":0.0,"end":4.21,"words":[[0.05,0.4],[0.4,0.63],[0.63,0.98],[0.98,1.67],[1.67,2.02],[2.42,2.77],[2.77,3.12],[3.12,3.47],[3.47,3.81],[3.81,4.16]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Most people have never watched a bill move.","start":5.01,"end":7.94,"words":[[5.07,5.44],[5.44,5.81],[5.81,6.03],[6.03,6.32],[6.32,6.69],[6.69,6.84],[6.84,7.06],[7.06,7.35]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Knowing the steps tells you exactly where your call, letter or visit can make a difference.","start":8.29,"end":14.51,"words":[[8.34,8.76],[8.76,8.93],[8.93,9.36],[9.36,9.69],[9.69,9.86],[9.86,10.54],[10.54,10.79],[10.79,10.96],[10.96,11.3],[11.6,11.94],[11.94,12.02],[12.02,12.44],[12.44,12.7],[12.7,13.04],[13.04,13.21],[13.21,13.88]]},{"el":"h0","text":"The steps","start":14.86,"end":15.88,"words":[[14.9,15.13],[15.13,15.69]]},{"el":"s0","text":"A member of the House or Senate introduces a bill, often with cosponsors, and it is referred to a committee: a CAREN Act would go to the House and Senate Judiciary Committees.","start":16.58,"end":27.27,"words":[[16.62,16.77],[16.77,17.14],[17.14,17.28],[17.28,17.43],[17.43,17.72],[17.72,17.8],[17.8,18.16],[18.16,18.97],[18.97,19.11],[19.11,19.41],[19.66,19.96],[19.96,20.18],[20.18,20.91],[21.17,21.39],[21.39,21.53],[21.53,21.68],[21.68,22.04],[22.04,22.19],[22.19,22.34],[22.34,22.85],[23.11,23.25],[23.25,23.62],[23.62,23.84],[23.84,24.06],[24.06,24.28],[24.28,24.42],[24.42,24.57],[24.57,24.86],[24.86,25.08],[25.08,25.45],[25.45,26.11],[26.11,26.69]]},{"el":"s0","text":"The committee chair decides whether to hold a hearing and a “markup,” where members debate and amend it.","start":27.62,"end":34.29,"words":[[27.67,27.83],[27.83,28.32],[28.32,28.64],[28.64,29.21],[29.21,29.54],[29.54,29.7],[29.7,30.11],[30.11,30.27],[30.27,30.76],[30.76,31.0],[31.0,31.17],[31.17,31.66],[31.66,31.9],[31.9,32.39],[32.39,32.88],[32.88,33.12],[33.12,33.53],[33.53,33.77]]},{"el":"s0","text":"If the committee approves it, leaders decide whether it gets a floor vote.","start":34.64,"end":39.47,"words":[[34.69,34.85],[34.85,35.01],[35.01,35.49],[35.49,35.97],[35.97,36.2],[36.48,36.88],[36.88,37.36],[37.36,37.68],[37.68,37.84],[37.84,38.16],[38.16,38.32],[38.32,38.55],[38.55,38.95]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In the Senate, most bills need 60 votes to end debate (the filibuster).","start":39.82,"end":45.53,"words":[[39.86,40.03],[40.03,40.2],[40.2,40.72],[41.02,41.45],[41.45,41.79],[41.79,42.05],[42.05,42.56],[42.56,42.99],[42.99,43.16],[43.16,43.42],[43.42,43.93],[43.93,44.1],[44.1,44.96]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Both chambers must pass identical text, and the president signs it or vetoes it; Congress can override a veto with two-thirds of each chamber.","start":45.88,"end":55.26,"words":[[45.93,46.23],[46.23,46.81],[46.81,47.1],[47.1,47.32],[47.32,48.05],[48.05,48.49],[48.75,48.97],[48.97,49.11],[49.11,49.77],[49.77,50.14],[50.14,50.28],[50.28,50.36],[50.36,50.8],[50.8,51.01],[51.27,51.78],[51.78,52.0],[52.0,52.59],[52.59,52.73],[52.73,53.1],[53.1,53.32],[53.32,53.76],[53.76,53.9],[53.9,54.12],[54.12,54.71]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Why most bills die","start":56.16,"end":57.95,"words":[[56.21,56.54],[56.54,57.08],[57.08,57.51],[57.51,57.83]]},{"el":"s1","text":"In recent Congresses, only a few percent of bills introduced became law (GovTrack).","start":58.65,"end":64.68,"words":[[58.7,58.86],[58.86,59.34],[59.34,60.13],[60.41,60.81],[60.81,60.97],[60.97,61.21],[61.21,61.69],[61.69,61.84],[61.84,62.16],[62.16,62.96],[62.96,63.44],[63.44,63.59],[63.59,64.23]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Most never get a hearing.","start":65.03,"end":66.64,"words":[[65.08,65.35],[65.35,65.58],[65.58,65.74],[65.74,65.85],[65.85,66.24]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Every bill that hasn't passed dies when a Congress ends and must be reintroduced; the 120th Congress begins on January 3, 2027.","start":66.99,"end":76.67,"words":[[67.04,67.31],[67.31,67.51],[67.51,67.71],[67.71,68.11],[68.11,68.37],[68.37,68.64],[68.64,68.84],[68.84,68.97],[68.97,69.44],[69.44,69.7],[69.7,69.9],[69.9,70.17],[70.17,70.3],[70.3,71.23],[71.46,71.6],[71.6,72.93],[72.93,73.39],[73.39,73.79],[73.79,73.92],[73.92,74.52],[74.52,74.79],[75.02,76.22]]},{"el":"s1","text":"The bills that move usually have a committee champion, cosponsors from both parties, outside endorsements, and constituents in key districts asking for them.","start":77.02,"end":87.44,"words":[[77.07,77.23],[77.23,77.53],[77.53,77.75],[77.75,77.98],[77.98,78.51],[78.51,78.74],[78.74,78.89],[78.89,79.34],[79.34,80.02],[80.29,80.97],[80.97,81.27],[81.27,81.57],[81.57,82.02],[82.29,82.82],[82.82,83.65],[83.91,84.14],[84.14,85.12],[85.12,85.27],[85.27,85.42],[85.42,86.1],[86.1,86.48],[86.48,86.63],[86.63,86.93]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Other ways a bill moves","start":88.34,"end":90.41,"words":[[88.39,88.73],[88.73,89.19],[89.19,89.42],[89.42,89.77],[89.77,90.22]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Small bills often pass by being folded into larger ones, such as a broader policing or civil rights package, or attached as an amendment.","start":91.11,"end":100.25,"words":[[91.16,91.46],[91.46,91.77],[91.77,92.08],[92.08,92.32],[92.32,92.55],[92.55,92.93],[92.93,93.48],[93.48,93.79],[93.79,94.17],[94.17,94.56],[94.83,95.14],[95.14,95.3],[95.3,95.45],[95.45,95.84],[95.84,96.38],[96.38,96.46],[96.46,96.84],[96.84,97.23],[97.23,97.77],[98.04,98.12],[98.12,98.58],[98.58,98.74],[98.74,98.89],[98.89,99.67]]},{"el":"s2","text":"A “companion” bill introduced in the other chamber lets both move at once.","start":100.6,"end":105.65,"words":[[100.64,100.8],[100.8,101.52],[101.52,101.76],[101.76,102.56],[102.56,102.71],[102.71,102.87],[102.87,103.11],[103.11,103.67],[103.67,103.99],[103.99,104.31],[104.31,104.55],[104.55,104.71],[104.71,105.1]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Hearings can also be requested on an issue, which builds a record even before a vote.","start":106.0,"end":112.4,"words":[[106.04,106.63],[106.63,106.89],[106.89,107.31],[107.31,107.47],[107.47,108.23],[108.23,108.4],[108.4,108.57],[108.57,108.91],[109.2,109.54],[109.54,109.96],[109.96,110.13],[110.13,110.55],[110.55,110.88],[110.88,111.22],[111.22,111.39],[111.39,111.81]]},{"el":"h3","text":"States move first","start":113.3,"end":115.02,"words":[[113.37,114.04],[114.04,114.38],[114.38,114.83]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Federal laws often follow state ones.","start":115.72,"end":118.92,"words":[[115.76,116.38],[116.38,116.64],[116.64,116.99],[116.99,117.43],[117.43,117.87],[117.87,118.31]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Oregon passed its law against racially biased police calls in 2019 after a lawmaker shared her own experience; California, New York and the city of San Francisco followed in 2020.","start":119.27,"end":132.32,"words":[[119.32,119.79],[119.79,120.09],[120.09,120.32],[120.32,120.48],[120.48,120.94],[120.94,121.48],[121.48,121.94],[121.94,122.33],[122.33,122.63],[122.63,122.79],[122.79,123.79],[123.79,124.1],[124.1,124.25],[124.25,124.79],[124.79,125.1],[125.1,125.25],[125.25,125.48],[125.48,126.48],[126.75,127.52],[127.79,128.02],[128.02,128.26],[128.26,128.49],[128.49,128.64],[128.64,128.95],[128.95,129.1],[129.1,129.33],[129.33,130.1],[130.1,130.56],[130.56,130.72],[130.72,131.72]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Each state law shows Congress the idea works and gives members a model.","start":132.67,"end":137.49,"words":[[132.72,132.96],[132.96,133.36],[133.36,133.53],[133.53,133.85],[133.85,134.41],[134.41,134.57],[134.57,134.97],[134.97,135.29],[135.29,135.53],[135.53,135.85],[135.85,136.33],[136.33,136.49],[136.49,136.97]]},{"el":"h4","text":"A path for a federal CAREN Act","start":138.39,"end":140.6,"words":[[138.43,138.6],[138.6,138.86],[138.86,139.03],[139.03,139.2],[139.2,139.8],[139.8,140.23],[140.23,140.49]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Find a House sponsor on the Judiciary Committee, and a Senate sponsor for a companion bill.","start":141.3,"end":147.14,"words":[[141.32,141.68],[141.68,141.83],[141.83,142.12],[142.12,142.55],[142.55,142.7],[142.7,142.84],[142.84,143.5],[143.5,144.01],[144.26,144.48],[144.48,144.63],[144.63,144.99],[144.99,145.43],[145.43,145.57],[145.57,145.72],[145.72,146.37],[146.37,146.66]]},{"el":"s4","text":"The map's allies layer shows committee members.","start":147.49,"end":150.71,"words":[[147.53,147.69],[147.69,148.01],[148.01,148.42],[148.42,148.74],[148.74,149.06],[149.06,149.55],[149.55,150.12]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Gather cosponsors from both parties.","start":151.06,"end":153.64,"words":[[151.11,151.41],[151.41,152.06],[152.06,152.35],[152.35,152.64],[152.64,153.08]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Ask your own members directly.","start":153.99,"end":156.33,"words":[[154.04,154.26],[154.26,154.4],[154.4,154.61],[154.61,155.04],[155.04,155.76]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Line up endorsements from civil rights, faith, law enforcement reform and business groups.","start":156.68,"end":163.15,"words":[[156.72,157.03],[157.03,157.19],[157.19,157.98],[157.98,158.3],[158.3,158.69],[158.69,159.17],[159.44,159.84],[160.12,160.27],[160.27,160.99],[160.99,161.38],[161.38,161.62],[161.62,162.09],[162.09,162.57]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Build the record: stories, 911 outcome data and city and state resolutions (toolkit).","start":163.5,"end":169.77,"words":[[163.54,163.81],[163.81,163.94],[163.94,164.33],[164.56,165.01],[165.24,166.48],[166.48,166.87],[166.87,167.2],[167.2,167.39],[167.39,167.65],[167.65,167.85],[167.85,168.18],[168.18,168.83],[168.83,169.28]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Ask for a hearing, or for the bill to be included in a larger package.","start":170.12,"end":174.88,"words":[[170.16,170.39],[170.39,170.55],[170.55,170.7],[170.7,171.24],[171.51,171.59],[171.59,171.74],[171.74,171.9],[171.9,172.13],[172.13,172.28],[172.28,172.44],[172.44,173.05],[173.05,173.21],[173.21,173.36],[173.36,173.75],[173.75,174.29]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Keep going in the states so the pressure grows from below.","start":175.23,"end":178.74,"words":[[175.25,175.46],[175.46,175.8],[175.8,175.93],[175.93,176.07],[176.07,176.48],[176.48,176.68],[176.68,176.82],[176.82,177.16],[177.16,177.5],[177.5,177.77],[177.77,178.18]]}]}